hadiths[77]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2205","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Food was brought to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) while he was at Marr az-Zahran. He said to Abu Bakr and 'Umar: ""Draw near and eat."" They said: ""We are fasting."" He said: ""Pack up for your two companions and work for your two companions! Draw near and eat."
"2206","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Count the crescent of Sha'ban for Ramadan, and do not mix with Ramadan unless that coincides with a fast one of you used to observe. And fast upon its sighting, and break the fast upon its sighting; if it is obscured from you, then the count is not obscured from you."
"2207","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""When Ramadan comes, the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of the Fire are closed, and the devils are shackled."
"2208","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'Adi bin Hatim, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to me: ""When Ramadan comes, fast thirty [days] unless you see the crescent before that."
"2209","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""If one of you hears the call and the vessel is in his hand, he should not put it down until he fulfills his need from it."
"2210","[AI-translation] He (peace be upon him) said: ""Proclaim among your people or among the people on the day of 'Ashura: Whoever has eaten, let him fast the remainder of his day (until night), and whoever has not eaten, let him fast."" It was reported from the hadith of Salama bin Al-Akwa' and .........."
"2211","[AI-translation] Narrated from 'Abdullah bin Unays that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""I was shown the Night of Al-Qadr, then I was made to forget it. And I was shown its morning, prostrating in water and clay."" He said: ""It rained on the night of the twenty-third, and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) led us in prayer. He turned away, and the trace of water and clay was on his forehead and nose."
"2212","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Hurayrah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""I was shown the Night of Al-Qadr, then some of my family woke me, and I forgot it. So seek it in the last ten."
"2213","[AI-translation] Narrated from Abu Sa'id, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) passed by a stream of water while he was on a mule, and the people were fasting, and the pedestrians were many. He said: ""Drink."" But they kept looking at him. He said: ""Drink, for I am the most lenient of you."" They kept looking at him, so he shifted his thigh and drank, and the people drank."
"2214","[AI-translation] From 'Ali that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten [nights] of Ramadan; if you are overcome, then do not be overcome concerning the remaining seven."
"2215","[AI-translation] From 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best fasting is the fasting of my brother Dawud; he used to fast one day and break his fast one day, and he would not flee when he met [the enemy]."
"2216","[AI-translation] Nu'man ibn Bashir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) turned his face towards the people and said: Straighten your rows three times. By Allah, you must straighten your rows or Allah will surely create discord among your hearts."
"2217","[AI-translation] From Anas ibn Malik who said: The prayer was established, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) turned his face towards us and said: Straighten your rows and stand close together, for I see you from behind my back."
"2218","[AI-translation] From Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas: He used to pray the last 'Isha' in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family), then he would perform Witr with one [rak'ah], not adding to it. It was said to him: Do you perform Witr with one, not adding to it, O Abu Ishaq? He said: Yes, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) say: The one who does not sleep until he performs Witr is a resolute person."
"2219","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, marfu'an: Verily, Allah has placed blessing in the suhur and in measuring."
"2220","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah and Abu Sa'id who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: Fasting is for Me, and I give its reward. The fasting person has two joys: when he breaks his fast he rejoices, and when he meets Allah he rejoices in his reward. By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad! The change in the breath of the fasting person is sweeter to Allah than the fragrance of musk."
"2221","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily, Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who partake of the suhur."
"2222","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, marfu'an: Verily, Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who partake of the suhur."
"2223","[AI-translation] 'As who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family) when a young man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, may I kiss while I am fasting? He said: No. Then an old man came and said: May I kiss while I am fasting? He said: Yes. He said: So some of us looked at each other, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The old man controls himself."
"2224","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar: That the people of Jahiliyyah used to fast the day of 'Ashura', and that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) fasted it and the Muslims before Ramadan was made obligatory. So when Ramadan was made obligatory, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Indeed, 'Ashura' is a day from the days of Allah, so whoever wishes may fast it, and whoever wishes may leave it."
"2225","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, marfu': ""If I remain alive, Allah willing, until next year, I will fast the ninth, fearing that the day of 'Ashura' might escape me."
"2226","[AI-translation] From Umm Hani': That the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) drank a drink and handed it to her to drink. She said: ""I am fasting, but I disliked returning your leftover."" He said: ""If it is a make-up fast from Ramadan, then make up a day in its place, and if it is a voluntary fast, then if you wish, make it up, and if you wish, do not make it up."
"2227","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, he said: A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) with a roasted rabbit, bringing its condiment with it, and placed it before him. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) refrained and did not eat, and his companions refrained and did not eat, and the Bedouin refrained. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""What prevents you from eating?"" He said: ""I fast three days of the month."" He said: ""If you are fasting, then fast the days of Al-Ghurr."" Meaning: Al-Ayyam Al-Bid."
"2228","[AI-translation] From Nafi', that 'Abdullah bin 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say on the day of 'Ashura': ""This is a day that the people of Jahiliyyah used to fast. So whoever wishes to fast it, let him fast it, and whoever wishes to leave it, let him leave it."
"2229","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik, he said: 'Ubadah bin Al-Samit informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) went out to inform about the Night of Al-Qadr, but two Muslim men quarreled. He said: ""I went out to inform you about the Night of Al-Qadr, but so-and-so and so-and-so quarreled, and it was raised. And perhaps that is better for you. Seek it in the seven, the nine, and the five."
"2230","[AI-translation] From Hamza bin 'Amr: That he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) about fasting while traveling? He said: ""Whichever of that is easier for you, do."
"2231","[AI-translation] Nasa'i did not say: from Abu Hurairah), he said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I see you fasting in a month in a way I have not seen you fast in any month like you fast in it."" He said: ""Which month?"" I said: ""Sha'ban."" He said: ""Sha'ban is between Rajab and Ramadan; people are heedless of it. The deeds of the servants are raised in it, and I love that my deed is not raised except while I am fasting."" He said: ""I see you fasting on Monday and Thursday, do you not leave them?"" He said: ""Indeed, the deeds of the servants..."" [the hadith]."
"2232","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah: From the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), he said: ""Beware of Al-Wisal"" - twice. It was said: ""You are practicing Al-Wisal?!"" He said: ""I spend the night while my Lord feeds me and gives me to drink. So commit yourselves to what you can bear of deeds."
"2233","[AI-translation] From Anas, marfu': ""Hasten the breaking of the fast, and delay the Suhur."
"2234","[AI-translation] Narrated Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the odd nights of the last ten of Ramadan."
"2235","[AI-translation] Araj: My grandmother told me that she entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) while he was eating lunch, and that was on a Saturday. He said: ""Come and eat."" She said: ""I am fasting."" He said to her: ""Did you fast yesterday?"" She said: ""No."" He said: ""Then eat, for fasting on a Saturday is neither for you nor against you."
"2236","[AI-translation] As: A man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Give me permission to castrate myself."" He (peace be upon him) said: ""The castration of my Ummah is fasting and Qiyam."
"2237","[AI-translation] Narrated Aisha: Hamza ibn Amr al-Aslami asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) saying: ""O Messenger of Allah! I am a man who fasts consecutively, so should I fast while traveling?"" He said: ""Fast if you wish, and break your fast if you wish."
"2238","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said: Fast upon seeing it, and break your fast upon seeing it. If clouds, darkness, or dust obstruct it, then complete the count. Do not anticipate the month, and do not connect Ramadan with a day from Shaban."
"2239","[AI-translation] Mulayh ibn Usamah, from his father, attributed to the Prophet (peace be upon him): Fast from brightness to brightness."
"2240","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas: A woman came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and mentioned to him that her sister had vowed to fast for a month, and that she traveled by sea and died without fasting. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to her: ""Fast on behalf of your sister."
"2241","[AI-translation] Narrated Muawiyah ibn Qurrat, from his father, from the Prophet (peace be upon him) who said: In fasting three days of the month is the fasting of a lifetime and its breaking of fast."
"2242","[AI-translation] Narrated Amir ibn Masud, attributed to the Prophet (peace be upon him): Fasting in winter is the cold booty."
"2243","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: The fast is the day you fast, and the Fitr is the day you break the fast, and the Adha is the day you sacrifice."
"2244","[AI-translation] Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib, from the Prophet (peace be upon him): Eat the suhur meal, for indeed it is the blessed meal."
"2245","[AI-translation] From 'Arfajah he said: I was in a house in which was 'Utbah ibn Farqad, and I wanted to narrate a hadith, but there was a man from the Companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who was more entitled to the hadith than me. So the man narrated from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) saying: In Ramadan, the gates of heaven are opened (in a narration: Paradise), and the gates of Hellfire are closed, and every rebellious devil is chained, and a caller calls out (in a narration: an angel) every night: O seeker of good, come forward, and O seeker of evil, restrain yourself."
"2246","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah: When he (peace be upon him and his family) tossed and turned during the night, he would say: There is no god but Allah, the One, the Subduer, the Lord of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them, the Almighty, the Oft-Forgiving."
"2247","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah: When he (peace be upon him and his family) prayed tahajjud, he would pronounce the salam between every two rak'ahs."
"2248","[AI-translation] From Sahl ibn Sa'd: When he (peace be upon him and his family) was fasting, he would order a man to mount an elevated structure, and when he said: The sun has set."
"2249","[AI-translation] From Anas: When he (peace be upon him and his family) was in residence, he would observe I'tikaf during the last ten days of Ramadan, and if he traveled, he would observe I'tikaf for twenty days the following year."
"2250","[AI-translation] From Anas: He (peace be upon him and his family) would not pray Maghrib while he was fasting until he broke his fast, even if with a sip of water."
"2251","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas: He (peace be upon him and his family) would not break his fast on the white days, neither while in residence nor while traveling."
"2252","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to be intimate with his wives while fasting, and then he would place a garment between him and her, meaning: the private parts."
"2253","[AI-translation] From Anas: He (peace be upon him and his family) would begin with dates when he broke his fast."
"2254","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to strive during the last ten [days] in a manner he did not strive at any other time."
"2255","[AI-translation] From Ibn Mas'ud: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to fast during travel and break his fast, and he would pray two rak'ahs, not abandoning them. He would say: ""One does not add to them."" Meaning the obligatory prayer."
"2256","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): He (peace be upon him and his family) used to break his fast with fresh dates before praying. If there were no fresh dates, then with dried dates. If there were none, he would take a few sips of water."
"2257","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah, she said: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to kiss while fasting and have physical contact while fasting, but he was the most capable among you of controlling his desire."
"2258","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to kiss me while he was fasting and I was fasting."
"2259","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, he said: There was a woman who prayed behind the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), one of the most beautiful of women. Some people would pray at the end of the men's rows and look at her. One of them would look at her from under his armpit (when he bowed), and one of them would advance to the first row so he would not see her. So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed this verse: ""And We have known those who advance among you, and We have known those who are left behind."" (24) [Al-Hijr]."
"2260","On the authority of ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Nuʿmān al-Suhaymī, who said: Qays ibn Ṭalq came to me in Ramaḍān during the last part of the night, after I had withdrawn my hands from the pre-dawn meal (suḥūr) for fear of dawn. He requested some food from me, so I said: ""O my uncle! If there had remained for you any portion of the night, I would have taken you to food and drink I have."" He said: ""You have it?"" So he entered, and I brought near to him tharīd (bread soaked in broth), meat, and nabīdh. He ate and drank, and he compelled me, so I ate and drank, while I was apprehensive of dawn. Then he said: Ṭalq ibn ʿAlī narrated to me that the Prophet of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Eat and drink, and let not the ascending white light deceive you; so eat and drink until the redness appears to you horizontally."""
"2262","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised [to the Prophet]: The Night of Decree is the twenty-seventh or twenty-ninth night, and the angels that night on earth are more numerous than pebbles."
"2263","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) did an act for which he took a concession. This reached some of his companions, and it was as if they disliked it and refrained from it. When this reached him, he stood to deliver a sermon and said: ""What is the matter with men who have heard of a matter for which I took a concession, so they dislike it and refrain from it? By Allah, I am the most knowledgeable of them regarding Allah, and the most fearful of Him."
"2264","[AI-translation] From Anas, raised [to the Prophet]: Whoever intends to fast, let him eat something for suhur."
"2265","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised [to the Prophet]: Whoever is overcome by vomiting does not have to make it up."
"2266","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas who said: It is of the Sunnah to eat [on the Day of Fitr] before going out, even with a single date."
"2267","[AI-translation] From Uqbah bin Amir that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah will distance Hell from him by a journey of a hundred years."
"2268","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah will place between him and the Fire a trench like that between the heaven and the earth."
"2269","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet, peace be upon him: How excellent is the pre-dawn meal of the believer, dates."
"2270","[AI-translation] From Anas, who said: He, peace be upon him and his family, forbade fasting six days of the year: the three days of Tashriq, the Day of Fitr, the Day of Adha, and the Day of Friday, specifically among the days."
"2271","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, forbade fasting on the Day of Friday except with days before it or after it."
"2272","[AI-translation] From Anas bin Malik that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: This Ramadan has come to you; in it the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained."
"2273","[AI-translation] From Khalid bin Madan who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Come to the blessed morning meal. Meaning: the pre-dawn meal."
"2274","[AI-translation] Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: O Messenger of Allah! I find in myself the strength to fast while traveling, is there any sin upon me? So the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: It is a concession from Allah, so whoever takes it, it is good; and whoever loves to fast, there is no sin upon him."
"2275","Kahmas al-Hilali narrated: ""I embraced Islam, so I came to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and informed him of my Islam. I stayed for a year, during which I became emaciated and my body wasted away. [Then I came to him again.] He lowered his gaze, then raised it. I said: 'Do you not recognize me?' He said: 'And who are you?' I said: 'I am Kahmas al-Hilali.' He said: 'What has brought you to the state I see?' I said: 'I have not broken my fast during the day since [meeting] you, nor have I slept at night.' He said: 'And who commanded you to torture yourself?! Fast the month of patience (Ramadan), and one day of every month.' I said: 'Increase me.' He said: 'Fast the month of patience, and two days of every month.' I said: 'Increase me, for I find strength.' He said: 'Fast the month of patience, and three days of every month.'"""
"2276","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: A woman must not fast a voluntary day outside of Ramadan while her husband is present except with his permission."
"2277","[AI-translation] Narrated Bashir: That he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family), ""Should I fast on Friday and not speak to anyone on that day?"" He said: ""Do not fast on Friday except within days of which it is one. As for not speaking to anyone, by my life, speaking what is good and forbidding evil is better than remaining silent."
"2278","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Umamah from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family): He said: ""Do not fast on Saturday except for an obligatory fast. And if you find nothing but the bark of a tree, then break your fast on it."
"2279","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah from the Prophet (peace be upon him): He said: ""A woman must not fast a voluntary fast outside of Ramadan while her husband is present except with his permission."
"2280","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Do not fast on Friday unless a day precedes it or a day follows it."
"2281","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir: That the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""There is no Wisal (continuous fasting) in fasting."
"2282","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah, elevated to the Prophet (peace be upon him): ""Nothing transmits anything to anything. Nothing transmits anything to anything,"" three times. A Bedouin stood up and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, a scab can be on the lip of a camel or on its rump, and it covers the camels with mange."" He remained silent for a while, then said: ""What infected the first one? There is no contagion, no Safar, and no Hama. Allah created every soul and wrote its life, its death, its afflictions, and its provision."
